  "name": "Amorfino (Montubio coastal sung couplets)",
  "family": "global",
  "lineage": "Improvised sung couplets of the Montubio people, the mestizo farmers and horsemen of Ecuador's coastal lowlands in Manabí, Los Ríos and Guayas. Amorfinos are short rhymed verses of love, wit and rural life, often traded as a challenge between a man and a woman or between rival singers, sung to a simple recurring tune with or without guitar, and they are held up as a core expression of Montubio identity.",
